mutual meaning others can follow them

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:22.600 align:start position:19%
back so people can follow each other but
naturally some users will end up being

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:26.480 align:start position:19%
more popular meaning with more followers
and this indicates that it will be a

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.039 align:start position:19%
read heavy system as most users only
browse the tweets while a small

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:33.960 align:start position:19%
percentage will be actively creating
these tweets and the typical tweet looks

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:39.399 align:start position:19%
something like this people can tweet
text up to 280 characters and optionally

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.879 align:start position:19%
they can also include images and videos
and we also have some interactions at

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.360 align:start position:19%
the bottom like users can comment
retweet or like other people's tweets

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.039 align:start position:19%
and now let's prioritize these features
and see which are the must have features

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:55.719 align:start position:19%
for us the core features that we will
focus on are the followings users need

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:59.760 align:start position:19%
to be able to follow other people we
will support the tweeting functionality

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:04.439 align:start position:19%
users need to be able to create tweets
and and this tweet length can be up to

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:08.759 align:start position:19%
280 characters for most users and we
will also support images and videos but

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:13.240 align:start position:19%
we won't be covering the premium feature
of extended tweet length in this basic

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.840 align:start position:19%
design so the maximum tweet length is
still 280 characters we will also

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:22.079 align:start position:19%
support the news feed users need to see
tweets from other users they follow and

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:26.200 align:start position:19%
on X for example we have the for you and
following feeds the for you feed is a

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:29.960 align:start position:19%
bit algorithmic while the following is
just showing the tweets of people that

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:33.479 align:start position:19%
you follow and we will only cover the
this type of Feed in our system design

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:37.280 align:start position:19%
with that let's move on to
non-functional requirements and let's

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:41.320 align:start position:19%
consider the scale and performance
demands of this system let's start with

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:46.360 align:start position:19%
the scale research shows that X
currently has 500 million monthly active

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:51.079 align:start position:19%
users and let's assume that out of these
200 million are daily active users and

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.960 align:start position:19%
the typical user here on average follows
around 4 100 people with this

00:01:53.119 --> 00:01:59.479 align:start position:19%
information we can calculate the read
and write volumes let's start with the

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:04.119 align:start position:19%
read volume with our assumption which is
typically daily active users read on

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:09.160 align:start position:19%
average 100 tweets per day that will be
around 200 Millions time 100 and we will

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:13.160 align:start position:19%
have 20 billion reads daily and when it
comes to the right volume we can assume

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:17.760 align:start position:19%
that daily active user typically creates
10 tweets per day significantly lower

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:22.599 align:start position:19%
than the read volume and that will be
200 Millions time 10 and that will be 2

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:26.920 align:start position:19%
billion new tweets daily in our system
and regarding the data size that will be

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:31.440 align:start position:19%
storing each of these tweets can be 1
kiloby on average if it's text only but

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:36.519 align:start position:19%
if it contains attachments like images
and videos then it can range from 1

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:40.200 align:start position:19%
megab to 5 mgab but to simplify let's
assume that an average tweet size will

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.959 align:start position:19%
be 1 megabytes even though some tweets
